    "At the locked-in $210/week ($910/month) tuition and 38 children, Year 2 operations show an operating margin of $112,354.23 before building and investor debt, with the owner as unpaid director. Owner-set budgets: food capped at $2,000.00/month (Missouri meal pattern still met); toiletries and cleaning within $300.00/month ($3,110.18/year with paper towels halved); classroom and office consumables halved to $1,599.87/year; utilities locked at $1,500.00/month; tax preparation $1,000.00/year; curriculum mapping $7,500.00 and native Spanish review $1,500.00, one-time, with no recurring curriculum or Spanish review fee; RN consultation $2,000.00/year; administration cut to $5,872.00/year (part-time bookkeeper); building upkeep handled in-house (lawn, HVAC service, electrical, parking and staff mobile removed; snow halved). Many costs are one-time: $142,554.00 one-time (months 1\u20137) vs $286,007.37/year recurring. Net cash turns positive in month 6; cumulative pilot cash turns positive in month 24 at the month-12 rate, before building payments and debt.",
